From a58f04aa69123cf56d4d47684e81baea96a7fa8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 18:52:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 510/913] drivers: stm32_cpu_opp: add STM32MP2 support

In STM32MP2 family the CA35SS DVFS operation required a specific
sequence to change the VDDCPU and Cortex-A35 clock and to control
the speed of memories inside Cortex-A35i sub system.

The sequence is implemented in the function set_opp() under the
CFG_STM32MP2x compilation flags.

The integration with SCPI PERF protocol in SCP for STM32MP2 family is
also prepared under CFG_SCPFW_MOD_DVFS compilation flag

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 7a10da8a09c0f340c84e82d12e71d17ad13dcd97 drivers: stm32_cpu_opp: add STM32MP2 support]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Id6770aa62fd14d18fd16535d74d18d89b281e438
